# Yosys cell-count estimate for mul48_kernel (ADR-0007 M4).
# Stops after techmap+stat: the bare `opt` after techmap hangs on the
# bit-blasted 32x64 multiplier (same opt_share-class grind seen in ABC),
# and no ECP5 mapping is needed (M4 target is SKY130 via LibreLane,
# whose own synth sequence is proven on the strictly-harder full core).
# Result: 106,555 primitive cells ($_AND_ 52k, $_XOR_ 34k, ...) =>
# ~15-25k sky130 cells, ~0.25 mm^2. Die sized from this in
# hdl/openlane/mul48/config.yaml.
# Pinned: Yosys 0.68 (oss-cad-suite).

read_verilog -sv ../rtl/fixed_pkg.sv
read_verilog -sv ../rtl/mul48_kernel.sv
hierarchy -check -top mul48_kernel
proc
opt
fsm
opt
memory
opt
techmap
opt_clean
stat
